# Milestone: M3
# Covers: two strands enqueued in FIFO order; scheduler dispatches them
#         in order A-then-B; both run to completion.
#
# defer-to: T39 + T20-promotion
#
# Reason: requires Strand.new urbiscript syntax to create multiple strands
# from within a chk fixture.  The chk runner is REPL-driven only — it has
# no host hook to call urbi_strand_create / urbi_strand_start for separate
# strands.  T20 ships the C API but not the urbiscript-level Strand.new
# binding; that promotion is tracked in T20-promotion (M4/M5 scope).
# T39 (chk runner extension) adds the ## host: driver mechanism needed to
# drive two strands from C and observe their scheduling order.
#
# When T39 + T20-promotion land, implement this fixture by:
#   1. Creating two strands via urbi_strand_create (host driver).
#   2. Starting both with urbi_strand_start (they enter READY state).
#   3. Stepping the VM: assert first strand runs before second (FIFO).
#
# Urbiscript source (activate at T39 + T20-promotion):
#   ## host: create strand A (body: echo("A")); create strand B (body: echo("B"))
#   ## host: step until quiescent
#   --- expected output ---
#   [00000001] "A"
#   [00000002] "B"
